      // "two representations disagree; which location, if any, should become current?" Different
      // subjects, evidence, resolution semantics and audit requirements. Sharing one table to satisfy a
      // "one proposals mechanism" principle would make the queue's resolution semantics generic too.
      //
      // ── NAMED SLOTS, NOT GENERIC CLAIMS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
      // The competing representations are differently TYPED — two are free text, and a third
      // (`assets.room_id`) is a Room entity id. A generic claims table would flatten an id and a name
      // into one column, which is the "one table meaning two things" this ruling rejects.
      //
